From 237cae4055a53bd0a86740b8ff8430e829590865 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: SovereignOS Build <build@sovereignos.local>
Date: Fri, 2 Oct 2026 19:23:37 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] airpods: add BluetoothDevice#setAirPodsAudioRoute behind
 MANAGE_AIRPODS_IDENTITY

The AirPods app has to take the AirPods out of the active audio slots when both
pods are out of the ears, and put them back, like an iPhone does. Granting it
MODIFY_AUDIO_ROUTING would let it redirect any app's audio, so add a narrow call
instead: only for a bonded device registered through setAirPodsIdentity, it
removes the device only from the A2DP/HFP slots where it is active, restores
only what it removed and only where the slot is still free, and never selects
another device. The record is dropped on profile disconnect, unbond and adapter
off, and the route is restored if the calling process dies.
