+    /**
+     * Takes this <em>bonded</em> device, which must currently be registered as an AirPods accessory
+     * through {@link #setAirPodsIdentity}, out of the active A2DP and HFP slots ({@code
+     * awayFromAirPods} true: the audio and any call play on the phone) or puts it back (false). Only
+     * a device that is the active device on a profile is removed from that profile, only what was
+     * removed is restored, and only where the slot is still free; no other device is ever selected.
+     * The route is also restored when the profile disconnects, the bond is removed, Bluetooth is
+     * turned off, or the calling process dies.
+     *
+     * <p>Requires {@code BLUETOOTH_CONNECT} and the signature|privileged permission {@code
+     * org.sovereignos.permission.MANAGE_AIRPODS_IDENTITY}, enforced in the Bluetooth service. Does
+     * not require {@code BLUETOOTH_PRIVILEGED} or {@code MODIFY_AUDIO_ROUTING}.
+     *
+     * @return true when the request was applied or there was nothing to do; false when refused or on
+     *     error
+     */
+    @Hide
+    @SystemApi
+    @RequiresBluetoothConnectPermission
